+
+### 4.3 list_conversations
+
+A client MAY ask for its conversation summaries with `{"type":"list_conversations"}`. The frame accepts an optional integer `limit` from 1 through 200 and an optional composite `before` cursor containing an ISO `updatedAt` and a `sessionId`; invalid values receive `INVALID_MESSAGE` ([validated by: accepts only a complete, bounded conversation-list request](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L91)).
+
+When `transport.history.enabled` is true, the server answers the request without entering the per-session turn queue with one `conversation_list` frame. It reads the user id from the authenticated connection, never from a frame field, calls the store with `{limit, before}` even when both are undefined, and serializes every summary time as an ISO string; it sends no `stream_end` ([validated by: sends the authenticated user only their ISO conversation summaries when history is enabled](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L107)).
+
+When history is not enabled, the server answers `list_conversations` with `UNSUPPORTED` rather than exposing a list ([validated by: refuses a list request with UNSUPPORTED until the deployer enables history](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L142)).
 
